1957 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Users can create events by specifying details such as the event title, date, time, duration, location, and description. They can also set recurring events, which is useful for daily, weekly, monthly, or custom recurring schedules. While Google Calendar primarily operates online, it offers limited offline access, allowing users to view and edit events even without an internet connection, with changes syncing once a connection is reestablished)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
